ntion to borderlands, bilingualism, labor, identity, and cultural production.", "children": [{"id": "5832c21f-a7bf-4aac-bbc6-800cbbd4bc24", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Migration systems", "children": [{"id": "6abff668-848a-4e67-bd1a-1923c88baad1", "type": "concept", "title": "Rural-urban migration and transnational households"}, {"id": "d3a9da5e-63bc-4b70-9dd9-d6b44a04b0da", "type": "concept", "title": "Exile, asylum, refugees, and economic migration"}, {"id": "94c6c686-0120-4fbb-907b-07569e6865ea", "type": "concept", "title": "Remittances, return migration, and circular mobility"}], "description": "Students study migration as produced by labor markets, policy, violence, family, and aspiration."}, {"id": "d679d775-f033-4ea5-a4b7-a5993ce0da22", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Borderlands and bilingual cultures", "children": [{"id": "b2a39c61-9d96-4be6-a9ed-dd444d0024be", "type": "concept", "title": "Chicano/a/x and Mexican American histories"}, {"id": "7b361e60-b8af-4c43-9496-3ae1d9012770", "type": "concept", "title": "Spanglish, code-switching, and translation"}, {"id": "3ba70699-6094-4d19-a6f7-09574d7857dc", "type": "concept", "title": "Border art, corridos, activism, and surveillance"}], "description": "This section frames the U.S.-Mexico border and other contact zones as cultural laboratories."}, {"id": "95d7d3ce-7afa-4856-8bd3-6be7094d5c05", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Diasporic cultural production", "children": [{"id": "f469c59d-fc26-475b-bcb5-fc0c37dd4e32", "type": "concept", "title": "Cuban, Dominican, Puerto Rican, Salvadoran, Colombian, and Venezuelan diasporas"}, {"id": "327ee73f-f705-498a-9834-8a5eca1a1408", "type": "concept", "title": "Literature, music, food, religion, and media"}, {"id": "4d165f4e-6adb-44dc-9653-61849fd61051", "type": "concept", "title": "Citizenship, identity, race, and generational change"}], "description": "Students learn how diaspora reshapes both home and host societies."}]}, {"id": "7ac2eacc-bec1-43e3-87b1-da1409ff53e2", "type": "topic", "title": "Contemporary Social Movements and Global Hispanic Futures", "description": "Analyzes feminist, Indigenous, environmental, student, labor, LGBTQ+, and anti-racist movements in relation to media, democracy, and globalization.", "children": [{"id": "15e9b9c7-587b-45f4-89db-fdaa93777797", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Feminist and LGBTQ+ movements", "children": [{"id": "2bf0fdc9-130e-4458-bd12-d83d5f35eeb2", "type": "concept", "title": "Ni Una Menos and anti-femicide activism"}, {"id": "d8e6c5b7-0478-4d3e-a9b3-cf802c13b896", "type": "concept", "title": "Reproductive rights and green-scarf movements"}, {"id": "007c8f63-22bf-4bba-aa3d-049c0acaa045", "type": "concept", "title": "Queer cultural production, policy, and backlash"}], "description": "Students connect culture to rights, embodiment, media activism, and law."}, {"id": "a1e4e7d6-5842-4ae7-9119-afcec9326e15", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Indigenous, environmental, and land struggles", "children": [{"id": "ea4355f9-a220-4a50-aa5c-902dff424afa", "type": "concept", "title": "Plurinationalism and constitutional debates"}, {"id": "87dccd43-7347-48cf-bcc4-62e2397d6695", "type": "concept", "title": "Mining, water, forests, and environmental conflict"}, {"id": "b1845150-0498-45f3-9f50-1e1dbc41be17", "type": "concept", "title": "Language revitalization and community media"}], "description": "This subtopic links language, territory, extraction, and climate justice."}, {"id": "af0e939e-11df-4085-8b10-4d5123bcac76", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Media, democracy, and globalization", "children": [{"id": "3e85df0a-8878-4f36-ac56-62ff9c0ea3c0", "type": "concept", "title": "Digital activism, misinformation, and censorship"}, {"id": "6cc73437-1609-463a-9fc6-f1cf9366300b", "type": "concept", "title": "Urban inequality, tourism, and cultural branding"}, {"id": "2ff7cd3f-f307-4f77-8247-8e8865279dfc", "type": "concept", "title": "Transnational pop culture, sports, and creative industries"}], "description": "Students analyze how contemporary Hispanic cultures circulate through platforms, markets, and political polarization."}]}, {"id": "acd08c50-6103-4684-9088-ef86bbf59e94", "type": "topic", "title": "Cultural Analysis Research Presentation", "description": "Culminates in a research-based interpretation of a cultural object, practice, site, movement, or debate using evidence and comparative context.", "children": [{"id": "0bce530e-ccef-47c1-9035-b23c242f22ba", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Research question and object selection", "children": [{"id": "c31a3d24-27d4-4ba4-9389-16d551efc54d", "type": "concept", "title": "Choosing an artifact, practice, site, movement, or debate"}, {"id": "bf2a535b-c985-4785-bf33-3ef762a5fe64", "type": "concept", "title": "Formulating a comparative or historical question"}, {"id": "a1cbca3f-1b7f-4d33-992d-808be288560e", "type": "concept", "title": "Defining scope, stakes, and key terms"}], "description": "Students learn to turn curiosity into a focused, evidence-based cultural inquiry."}, {"id": "51eef8ba-7ef2-4bba-98b4-dc055e242e91", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Evidence and interpretation", "children": [{"id": "d2e3dbe2-d71a-44f3-a4fe-2f89fa2208d6", "type": "concept", "title": "Primary sources, images, interviews, statistics, and media texts"}, {"id": "408d8a5c-b312-429c-a30e-8445d76cfd43", "type": "concept", "title": "Scholarly sources and citation practice"}, {"id": "93bca4cb-3466-4579-97e7-bedd7ad3b59b", "type": "concept", "title": "Context, close analysis, and counter-interpretation"}], "description": "This subtopic trains students to support claims with primary and secondary materials."}, {"id": "e77ed3e2-6efe-4e21-94b4-2046f0e30032", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Presentation and reflection", "children": [{"id": "f927d513-006f-457f-9580-db4fd51be217", "type": "concept", "title": "Thesis, structure, visuals, and delivery"}, {"id": "0ea0b5eb-ff7d-4be7-8899-ced03b2242bc", "type": "concept", "title": "Audience questions and scholarly humility"}, {"id": "d3423cdc-b466-47be-bd3f-6d111d180fde", "type": "concept", "title": "Reflection on language, positionality, and ethical representation"}], "description": "Students practice public scholarship by communicating a nuanced argument clearly."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$hccvjson$::jsonb,
